tement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:81e223a5b2c3ae566a851669aaa2660fa2175faa4dcf870d22446b3635bf3cd1","file":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-Direct-Finiteness-Conjecture-in-Characteristic-Two-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":8,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"70efa57f0aaf913bd10a10387a27155bffa43fbb4865f85a262215a511953501","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-Direct-Finiteness-Conjecture-in-Characteristic-Two-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:81e223a5b2c3ae566a851669aaa2660fa2175faa4dcf870d22446b3635bf3cd1","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-Direct-Finiteness-Conjecture-in-Characteristic-Two-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L8"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere exist a finite field $K$ of characteristic two, a finitely presented group $G$ containing an element of odd prime order, and elements $a_{\\mathrm{out}},b_{\\mathrm{out}}\\in K[G]$ such that\n\\[\na_{\\mathrm{out}}b_{\\mathrm{out}}=1,\n\\qquad b_{\\mathrm{out}}a_{\\mathrm{out}}\\ne1.\n\\]\nThe field, group, and finite sums are specified by a terminating prescription involving finite sets and finite-field arithmetic."}
